# Workflow

Day to day you `run` the app, `view` a component, and `inspect` lowering.
Command flags live in the [CLI](/docs/reference/cli/).

## Run

```sh
rocci run examples/rocci/standalone/counter
rocci run examples/rocci/standalone/counter --no-window
rocci run examples/rocci/standalone/counter --no-live-reload
```

`--no-window` prints a URL; the HTTP origin is the same as the preview
webview. `--no-live-reload` pauses automatic refresh; watch still
rebuilds. `--log-handlers` prints matched routes.

## View

```sh
rocci view examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello --arg name=Ada
rocci browse examples/rocci/standalone/styling
```

`view` ignores HTTP declarations. `browse` is the component gallery.

## Inspect

```sh
rocci inspect examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
rocci inspect --ast examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

`inspect` always prints source-map segments. `--ast` adds the
S-expression tree.

## Editors and rocci-ops

Editor support is **current** in this repository. There is no Marketplace
install path yet. The server binary is `rocci-language-server`
(`cargo build -p rocci-rocdown-lsp`). Opening a `.rocci` file should show
diagnostics and semantic highlighting. After `uv run rocci-ops package
vscode`, install the `.vsix` with `uv run rocci-ops install vscode` or
`uv run rocci-ops install cursor`.

`uv run rocci-ops` also runs `check`, `install`, `promote-branch`, CI
helpers, and container sketches under `docker/`.

In the preview window, open Dev. **Performance**, **Source**, and
**Console** are host tools. Console shows runtime lines and teed Roc
stderr, not `@component` logs.

Next: [Package](/docs/applications/package/).
